{"id": 64, "ts": 1780426732.8488412, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fB can be uncooperative and sometimes comes across as grumpy. Those traits directly undermine the crew\u2011cooperation and professional\u2011communication criteria that are essential for long\u2011distance operations. While B\u2019s technical strengths\u2014high conscientiousness, strong stress handling, excellent weather assessment and computer skills\u2014are valuable, the lack of reliable teamwork makes the overall risk profile higher.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC, despite having some communication difficulty and being perceived as egocentric, consistently puts concern for others above everything and makes correct decisions quickly. The \u201cconcern for others\u201d signal suggests a willingness to prioritize crew safety and collaboration, which can offset the communication weakness if supported by proper cockpit resource management training.\nGiven the current evidence, I am shifting my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**. I believe C\u2019s decision quality, attention to detail, and evident concern for teammates provide a more balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role than B\u2019s strong technical profile paired with notable cooperation concerns."}
