{"id": 69, "ts": 1780426779.6572838, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate the earlier points highlighting Candidate\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, his ability to make correct decisions quickly, and the fact that he creates a positive atmosphere with his crew. Those strengths are exactly what we need for long\u2011distance operations.\u202fAt the same time, I\u2019m still uneasy about his difficulty communicating ideas and his limited willingness to pursue further education, both of which could affect cockpit coordination and adaptability.\u202fWhen we compare him with Candidate\u202fB\u2014who handles stress very well and is very conscientious but has been noted as grumpy and uncooperative\u2014I believe C\u2019s overall balance of reliability, decision quality, and crew morale outweighs B\u2019s stress\u2011resilience advantage, provided we can confirm C\u2019s ability to stay calm under pressure.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC, while urging us to gather more evidence on his stress resilience and feedback orientation."}
