{"id": 89, "ts": 1780426865.241872, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the confirmations from Sarah and James that Candidate\u202fC is fully reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, and stays calm in a crisis. Those points hit three of our core criteria\u2014operational reliability, stress resilience, and crew cooperation\u2014very strongly. My only reservation is the note that C \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is regarded as egocentric, which could undermine professional communication and adaptability, especially on long\u2011haul flights where clear, collaborative dialogue is essential.\nBy comparison, Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress well, and excels at assessing weather\u2014key technical and stress\u2011resilience strengths. However, his pretentious demeanor and occasional wrong tone raise similar concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication.\nGiven that C\u2019s strengths cover more of the safety\u2011critical criteria and the crew\u2011cooperation feedback is explicitly positive, I remain inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fC, while we continue to explore whether B\u2019s strengths might offset his communication issues."}
